@startuml 04-blocked-user-next-request
!include _style.iuml
title What a blocked user's next request sees (no event involved)
autonumber

actor "Blocked user" as U
participant "JWTFilter" as F
participant "BlockedTokenService\n(cache blockedTokens)" as BT
participant "CustomUserDetailsDaoService\n(cache authUsers, 60 s)" as UD
database "users" as DB
participant "Security entry point" as EP

U -> F : any request with BLINKSTAY_TOKEN cookie
F -> F : verify signature and expiry
F -> BT : token logged out?
BT --> F : no
F -> UD : loadAuthSnapshot(userId)
UD -> DB : on cache miss only
note right of UD
  Blocking cleared authUsers,
  so this is a fresh read.
end note
UD --> F : enabled = isActive && deletedAt == null\n-> false
F -> F : save reason ACCOUNT_BLOCKED,\nclear the cookie,\ncontinue as anonymous
F -> EP : protected URL needs a login
EP --> U : 401 { code: "ACCOUNT_BLOCKED" }
note over U
  The frontend clears its state and
  shows the "account blocked" page.
  Public pages still work.
end note
@enduml
